#: ../../guide/flags.rst:3
msgid "Flags"
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/flags.rst:5
msgid "Flags are small pieces of metadata attached to a handler *at registration time* and readable from middlewares, other handlers of the same dispatch, and utility code. Where middlewares inject per-update data, flags carry per-handler configuration."
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/flags.rst:11
msgid "Declaring flags"
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/flags.rst:13
msgid "The global ``flags`` object (exported from :mod:`aiorubi`) generates a flag decorator for any attribute name:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/flags.rst:24
msgid "``flags.<name>`` with no call simply marks the handler with ``{\"<name>\": True}``. To attach a value, call the decorator:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/flags.rst:34
msgid "Keyword form builds an :class:`AttrDict` value — useful for grouped settings:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/flags.rst:42
msgid "The decorator is chainable: multiple ``@flags.*`` lines stack, and re-declaring the same name replaces its value."
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/flags.rst:45
msgid "Flags may also be attached to any callable — class-based handlers included:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/flags.rst:55
msgid "Reading flags"
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/flags.rst:57
msgid "Three helpers live in :mod:`aiorubi.dispatcher.flags`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/flags.rst:59
msgid "``extract_flags(obj)`` — all flags of a handler."
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/flags.rst:60
msgid "``get_flag(handler, name, default=None)`` — one flag."
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/flags.rst:61
msgid "``check_flags(handler, magic)`` — query flags with a magic-filter expression, e.g. ``check_flags(handler, F.admin_only)``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/flags.rst:64
msgid "Inside a middleware the handler object is available under the ``\"handler\"`` key of ``data``:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/flags.rst:76
msgid "Because flags are stored on the handler object (``handler.flags``), they cost nothing per update until read."
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/flags.rst:80
msgid "Built-in flag usage"
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/flags.rst:82
msgid "Filters can contribute flags at registration time: :class:`~aiorubi.filters.command.Command` appends itself to the ``commands`` flag (``update_handler_flags``) — used by command-listing tooling."
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/flags.rst:86
msgid "The ``chat_action`` flag is recognised by aiogram-compatible tooling; aiorubi does not ship a built-in runner for it (no chat-action API on Rubika), but the flag slot is reserved."
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/flags.rst:91
msgid "Writing flag-driven extensions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/flags.rst:93
msgid "Flags shine when combined with middlewares or the observer registry to build conventions:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/flags.rst:112
msgid "Notes and pitfalls"
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/flags.rst:114
msgid "Flag names must not start with an underscore — ``flags._private`` raises :class:`AttributeError`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/flags.rst:116
msgid "``@flags.x`` and ``@flags.x(...)`` both return the original callable, so flag decorators never change the handler's signature or break :doc:`argument injection <handlers>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/flags.rst:119
msgid "Flags are registration-time only: changing them at runtime means mutating ``handler.flags`` directly (supported, but unusual)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/flags.rst:121
msgid "Order with the observer decorator matters — put ``@dp.new_message(...)`` *above* the flags so the flags are already attached when the handler is registered (decorators apply bottom-up)."
msgstr ""

